<title>UK: Copper hits one-month high.</title>
<headline>Copper hits one-month high.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three month copper futures rose to a one-month high of $1,985 a tonne in afternoon trading on the London Metal Exchange (LME) on Friday, up $26 from Thursday's afternoon close.</p>
<p>Traders said the market rose on a combination of bullish factors including technical tightness in nearby copper supply, next week's key September LME options declaration and supply disruptions at two small facilities -- in Namibia and Chile.</p>
